      <h2>Understanding Payment Processing for Research Peptides</h2>

      <p>
        Businesses selling research-use-only peptides may encounter
        additional payment processing requirements. Payment providers
        evaluate the products being sold, website disclosures, business
        documentation, and the overall risk profile before making
        an underwriting decision.
      </p>

      <p>
        A provider that understands the business model can help merchants
        identify the documentation and operational requirements relevant
        to their application. Approval is subject to underwriting and
        the provider's applicable policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Choosing a Merchant Account</h2>

      <p>
        When evaluating a merchant account, businesses should review
        supported payment methods, processing fees, settlement terms,
        reserve requirements, integration options, and ongoing compliance
        obligations. These details can differ between providers and
        individual merchant agreements.
      </p>

      <h2>Website Transparency and Compliance</h2>

      <p>
        Clear product descriptions, accessible policies, accurate
        business information, and appropriate research-use disclosures
        can help a business present its operations for review. Merchants
        should describe their products and intended uses accurately
        and comply with applicable laws and provider requirements.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Important:</strong> A research-use-only disclaimer does
        not automatically make a product or business eligible for
        payment processing. Each application is assessed individually.
      </div>

